      "gitCommit": {
        "shortHash": "23ecd35",
        "hash": "23ecd35faec53753720e778e604b4dfd0bf5edc5",
        "subject": "Show investment accounts and stop gating types on parser support",
        "body": "Show investment accounts and stop gating types on parser support\n\nAdds `investment` to the account and transaction type unions so the app\ncan render what the API now returns: brokerage rows carry the new type,\nand the accounts screens need an icon, colour and label for it. The\naccount-type union was duplicated across five files, so it is now defined\nonce in `api/bankAccounts.ts` and imported.\n\nSeparately, fixes a bug a user hit: creating a Banorte *credit* account\nwas impossible in the app. `availableTypes` narrowed the type buttons from\n`bank.supported_type`, and Banorte is `debit` in production, so the credit\nbutton never rendered.\n\n`supported_type` means \"we have a hand-written parser for this bank and\ntype\" — a statement about our parsing capability, not about which accounts\na person may own. Nothing server-side rejects such an account, and web\nnever gated on it. Only the app did. It now offers every type for any\nbank, matching web; anything without a dedicated parser is read by AI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1786941252000
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1786941252000
        },
        "branch": "HEAD"
      },
